Package: amber-theme
Version: @VERSION@-1
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Hyperquader <hyperquader@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: hicolor-icon-theme, mint-y-icons, yaru-theme-icon, librsvg2-common
Recommends: cinnamon, nemo-python
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/Hyperquader-Coders/amber-theme
Description: Amber Linux — 1980s amber-phosphorus Cinnamon/GTK theme suite
 A Cinnamon/GTK theme built around the warm amber glow of 1980s phosphor CRT
 monitors. Every colour in every shell component traces back to a handful of
 primitive tokens per profile, so the same architecture drives five distinct
 looks: phosphorus (dark), Amber-Light, Amber-Kat800, Amber-Katai and
 Amber-Mint.
 .
 Bundles GTK 3, GTK 4, libadwaita, Cinnamon shell styling, a Metacity/Muffin
 window-border theme, per-profile folder icon themes with Nemo folder-colour
 integration, and ten amber-phosphor desktop wallpapers.
 .
 Forked from Linux Mint's Mint-Y-Dark-Grey (GTK/Cinnamon) and recoloured
 folder icons from Yaru / Mint-Y-Yaru — the base icon themes remain a runtime
 dependency since only the folder art is overridden, everything else falls
 through via Inherits=.
